{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Rav, yet Joseph my son lives.</b> Meaning: Jacob called 'rav' the one who brought the wagons, like 'rav ha-chovel.' And he asked him: 'Is Joseph my son yet alive?' — for I trust you more than them. Another explanation: his sons were lengthy in their words and recounting to him the greatness of Joseph; therefore he said to them, 'rav — enough for you to tell of this.' He only said: 'If my son lives in truth'; and if true, 'I will go and see him,' etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 45, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:07:09.543144978Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}